  "_readme": "Every sound the game asks for, by cue id (docs/design/audio.md). Kind sfx files are variants in content/audio/sfx (one plays at random); music and ambient files are a track's stems in content/audio/music or content/audio/ambient, base layer first, the same length and sample rate. File names follow the pipeline's naming contract (Pipeline/README.md). GainDb is the cue's level over its normalised file. Haptic (light, medium, selection or empty) is the pulse the cue brings when haptics are on. A cue whose files do not exist yet plays nothing.",
